{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X1QJAuChnTEqAwsTThicfC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"54e48e8f97ee116b97829f2b9df66c699d27dd4d","date":"2026-09-29T10:07:27+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop loading code the patient chart summary doesn't use (#3712)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Stop loading code the patient chart summary doesn't use\n\nRegister the growth chart dashboard page with getAsyncLifecycle, so it\nonly loads when someone opens the growth chart.\n\nIt was registered with getSyncLifecycle, which put the page and\neverything it imports into the code the module loads as soon as it\nstarts. Rendering the Growth chart link in the left nav starts the\nmodule, so every patient chart load also downloaded Carbon Charts and\n338 KiB of chart CSS. The module now loads 2 KiB up front instead of\n533 KiB.\n\n* Lazy-load the vitals and biometrics charts\n\nLoad the vitals and biometrics chart components with React.lazy when\nsomeone switches to the chart view, showing the same inline loading\nindicator as the vitals header while they load.\n\nBoth widgets show a table by default, but they imported their chart\ncomponents directly, so @carbon/charts-react loaded with the patient\nsummary whether or not anyone opened a chart. The chart view tests now\nwait for the chart to load. The vitals module now loads 207 KiB up front\ninstead of 559 KiB.\n\n* Register the procedures form workspace asynchronously\n\nRegister the procedures form workspace with getAsyncLifecycle, like the\nother 20 workspaces in this repo.\n\nWith getSyncLifecycle, zod and react-hook-form loaded as soon as the\nProcedures link rendered in the left nav. The procedures module now\nloads 18 KiB up front instead of 121 KiB.\n\n* Don't share lodash-es from the patient chart app\n\nRemove lodash-es from esm-patient-chart-app's peerDependencies and keep\nit as a regular dependency, so the build only bundles the functions the\napp imports.\n\nListing it as a peer dependency made it a shared module. The app shell\ndoesn't provide lodash-es, so the chart app always loaded its own copy,\nand the build can't drop unused code from a shared module, so that copy\nwas the whole package (77 KiB) for the three functions the app uses.\n\n---------","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"00b9a23a7a7cf02b34791dca2c8e495db24f818b","date":"2026-09-20T22:23:25+03:00","message":"(docs) Fix growth chart and procedures README links","refs":"","body":"Update the growth chart resources to the current O3 documentation. Point\nthe procedures configuration link to the guide for configuring\nindividual frontend modules.\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T23:29:42+03:00","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers are now named 'Edit or delete procedure' and 'Attachment actions', so the specs can no longer find them by 'Options'.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6e8da1b1b5a459933ca78eaabf87713592f5ab61","date":"2026-06-23T17:22:29+05:30","message":"(fix) Update Default Procedure Status Concept (#3412)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"45b86fe90224fd711b30831493509bea47627b89","date":"2026-06-04T21:58:13+05:30","message":"(chore) Add transifex config for the Procedures app (#3355)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"05f99be739478393ec4327bcb1f35126e7323f47","date":"2026-06-04T20:48:01+05:30","message":"(feat) Remove procedure overview widget (#3354)","refs":"","body":"Remove the ProceduresOverview component and its associated extension registration,\nconfiguration option, and test file. The detailed summary view is the primary\nprocedures display going forward.","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"84c21d9cc34e669f47a901457db4f5bdcb757943","date":"2026-06-03T22:43:21+03:00","message":"(fix) Render procedures form validation errors via Carbon invalid props (#3350)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"7e9e5ee856918aadc24ef5166218dec3fc800a62","date":"2026-05-28T03:12:35+05:30","message":"(test) O3-5655: Add E2E for procedure app (#3338)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dilan Kavishka","authorEmail":"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a19673101f1bb57cc88871e633733b5a6da6dbb9","date":"2026-05-26T22:43:54+03:00","message":"Remove feat/procedure-history from E2E workflow branch triggers","refs":"","body":"The feat/procedure-history branch was accidentally left in the push and\npull_request branch filters in .github/workflows/e2e.yml when PR #3320\nwas merged. This removes the stale branch reference, restoring the\noriginal trigger configuration.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6797e139e35959962c51b4148213d88ccdc94af7","date":"2026-05-26T19:38:03+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5077: Support recording clinical procedures (#3320)","refs":"","body":"* Update pull request branches in CI workflow\n\nRemove main branch restriction from pull requests.\n\n* Remove 'patch/*' branch from CI trigger\n\n* Update CI workflow to include additional branches\n\n* Add esm-patient-procedures-app to patient-chart monorepo\n\n* Refactor the file structure\n\n* Add feat/procedure-history branch to workflow triggers\n\n* Modify E2E test triggers for additional branches\n\nUpdated branch filters for E2E tests on push and pull request events.\n\n* Make concept sources configurable\n\n* Load durations dynamically\n\n* Make the form wider\n\n* Make the duration unit combo box\n\n* Make status a combo box\n\n* (fix) O3-5656: Make submit buttons sticky on procedure history form (#3290)\n\n* Fix: stick the submit buttons in procedure form\n\n* Fix: update procedures-form.workspace.test.tsx to new ComboBox components\n\n* (fix) O3-5657: Various fixes to the procedures form (#3297)\n\n* (fix) O3-5653: Wire body site and status concepts in config schema (#3313)\n\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Jayasanka Weerasinghe <33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Cleanup the file structure\n\n* Migrate to vitest\n\n* Fix the workspace\n\n* Isolate date time component\n\n* Prevent future 'any' types\n\n* Convert all function declarations to arrow functions\n\n* Fix accessibility issues in ConceptSearchField (#15)\n\n* Clear slected concep when changing value\n\n* Re-enable delete button after failed delete\n\nsetIsDeleting(false) was missing from the catch block, leaving\nthe Delete button permanently disabled after a transient error.\nUser had to close and reopen the modal to retry.\n\nAlso updates the test assertion to verify the button is re-enabled\nafter an error so the user can retry without reopening the modal.\n\n* docs: add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Enable delete button on error\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Add separate pagination configs for overview and detailed view\n\n* Align import order and type placement with O3 coding conventions\n\n* Add unit tests for ConceptSearchField and ProceduresActionMenu (#21)\n\n* Add test cases for procedures form component\n\n* Rename close workspace\n\n* Add translations to zod schema\n\n* Minor cleanups\n\n* Reset workflows\n\n* Remove unused abort controller\n\n* Update routes\n\n* Fix the overvierw URL\n\n* Add backend dependancies\n\n* fix: convert type-only imports to 'import type' syntax in procedures-app\n\nConvert all type-only imports in the procedures-app package to use\nthe 'import type' syntax instead of inline 'type' prefixes. This\nimproves code consistency and clarity.\n\nUpdated files:\n- procedures.resource.ts\n- dashboard.meta.ts\n- components/**/*.tsx\n- workspaces/procedures-form/**/*.tsx\n\nAddressed in PR #3320 review comment.\n\n* Remove selectedConcept from hook, use RHF as UUID source of truth\n\n* Surface hook errors in the UI\n\n* Address remaining PR review comments from denniskigen\n\n* Set date boundaries\n\n* Update config descriptions\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dilan Kavishka <109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"}],"totalCount":10}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2a84106-9760-4246-9f49-0b3af5163179","uuid":"013b81f5-3a95-48c1-b0f9-b82a0ac9c644","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:51:08.937Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"54e48e8f97ee116b97829f2b9df66c699d27dd4d","date":"2026-09-29T10:07:27+03:00","message":"(fix) Stop loading code the patient chart summary doesn't use (#3712)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Stop loading code the patient chart summary doesn't use\n\nRegister the growth chart dashboard page with getAsyncLifecycle, so it\nonly loads when someone opens the growth chart.\n\nIt was registered with getSyncLifecycle, which put the page and\neverything it imports into the code the module loads as soon as it\nstarts. Rendering the Growth chart link in the left nav starts the\nmodule, so every patient chart load also downloaded Carbon Charts and\n338 KiB of chart CSS. The module now loads 2 KiB up front instead of\n533 KiB.\n\n* Lazy-load the vitals and biometrics charts\n\nLoad the vitals and biometrics chart components with React.lazy when\nsomeone switches to the chart view, showing the same inline loading\nindicator as the vitals header while they load.\n\nBoth widgets show a table by default, but they imported their chart\ncomponents directly, so @carbo